    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152-a15">

                <pb facs="0559" n="437" xml:id="pg437"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 15 in No. 1049.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            White</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1887-09-16T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1887-09-15T00:00:00-05:00">undated</date>.] Received at
                        Shelburne, September 16, 1887.<lb/>Dated,
                        <placeName>Ottawa</placeName>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The matter not in my department. Have seen McLelan, who is acting for minister of
                    customs. He has telegraphed decision.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. S. D. Thompson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister of Justice.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
